# Engine warnings this project has decided to live with (tools/ci/**).
#
# One POSIX ERE per line, matched against the whole log line as the engine
# printed it. `#` starts a comment and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Rules for this file:
#   * an entry here is a RECORDED acceptance, not a filter that hides output.
#     Every warning line is still printed on every run (labelled as accepted);
#     `--strict-warnings` only stops failing on the listed shapes;
#   * add an entry only with a reason, in the comment above it, that says why
#     the warning is benign for this project. A warning whose cause is unknown
#     (the open R7 item: "Jolt Physics job system exceeded the maximum number of
#     jobs ...") must NOT be accepted here -- it is exactly what CI has to see;
#   * keep the patterns narrow. A pattern that matches a whole class of engine
#     output would silently disable the strict mode for that class.

# tools/tick_probe and tools/jolt_inventory are separate nested Godot projects
# (each has its own project.godot). The engine ignores them when importing this
# project and says so on every import. Expected and correct: neither folder is
# part of this project's content, and neither warning is a physics failure --
# the substring "jolt" in the jolt_inventory path must not be mistaken for one
# of the five Jolt physics warnings (hosted run 45921573623).
^WARNING: Detected another project\.godot at res://tools/tick_probe\. The folder will be ignored\.$
^WARNING: Detected another project\.godot at res://tools/jolt_inventory\. The folder will be ignored\.$
